1
00:00:29,623 --> 00:00:31,039
做好面对一切的准备
Be ready for anything.

2
00:00:31,789 --> 00:00:33,414
我们不知道Penny现在是什么状态
We don't know what state Penny is in.

3
00:00:33,456 --> 00:00:35,998
如果那些小混蛋敢和她一起去
If any of those brats have the nerve to come with her,

4
00:00:36,039 --> 00:00:37,998
我们就马上把他们放倒
we put them down immediately.

5
00:00:38,039 --> 00:00:39,664
将军下了死命令
The General gave his terms.

6
00:00:39,914 --> 00:00:40,956
不许节外生枝
No more games.

7
00:00:42,539 --> 00:00:43,998
有什么问题吗?
Is there a problem?

8
00:00:44,623 --> 00:00:48,414
只是 在回想我们走过来的每一步
Just, retracing the steps that led us here.

9
00:00:52,539 --> 00:00:53,539
怎么了 长官?
What is it, Sir?

10
00:00:54,164 --> 00:00:57,123
克罗 和罗宾 他们在学校机库
Qrow and Robyn, they're in the academy hanger.

11
00:00:57,331 --> 00:00:58,873
想要阻止炸弹被送出去?
Trying to stop the payload?

12
00:00:58,914 --> 00:01:00,706
或者只是想找条路出去
Or just looking for a way out.

13
00:01:00,748 --> 00:01:02,748
不会发生这样的事了
Not going to happen.

14
00:01:02,789 --> 00:01:05,164
我等不及给他俩来几枪了
I've been waiting to take my shot at those two.

15
00:01:05,581 --> 00:01:06,873
黄金特工们 我们走吧
Let's go, Ace Ops!

16
00:01:06,914 --> 00:01:09,414
但是有人得和将军一起留在这里
But someone needs to stay here with the General.

17
00:01:09,456 --> 00:01:10,331
我留下来吧
I'll stay.

18
00:01:11,206 --> 00:01:13,414
我们要是丢了炸弹 就失去了优势
We lose the payload, we lose our leverage.

19
00:01:13,539 --> 00:01:14,206
她说得没错
She's right.

20
00:01:14,873 --> 00:01:16,914
马上去抓住他们
Contain it. Now.

21
00:01:22,289 --> 00:01:25,123
长官 这次行动方针是...
Sir, this course of action-

22
00:01:25,164 --> 00:01:27,998
我希望你不要试图说服我
hope you're not going to try to talk me out of

23
00:01:30,831 --> 00:01:31,914
不会的 长官
No, Sir.

24
00:01:32,456 --> 00:01:33,748
我不认为这事有可能
I don't think that's possible.

25
00:01:39,998 --> 00:01:41,706
我还以为你不会真的一个人来
I didn't think you'd actually come alone.

26
00:01:44,289 --> 00:01:46,956
我还以为你的朋友们至少会有些抵抗
I expected at least some resistance from your friends.

27
00:01:47,664 --> 00:01:49,914
我不想任何人死
I don't want anyone else to die.

28
00:01:50,748 --> 00:01:52,331
我必须打开宝库
I must open the Vault.

29
00:02:01,331 --> 00:02:03,623
你做了正确的事
You've done the right thing

30
00:02:05,123 --> 00:02:06,039
没错
I have.

31
00:02:07,206 --> 00:02:08,164
感觉怪怪的
Feels weird.

32
00:02:30,748 --> 00:02:31,914
停!
Stay!

33
00:03:01,248 --> 00:03:03,956
对不住了 我们并不想打架
Sorry guys, but we don't wanna fight.

34
00:03:04,414 --> 00:03:06,498
我们也不能丟下擎天不管
We didn't wanna drop Atlas either,

35
00:03:06,914 --> 00:03:09,456
但是我们总得做些艰难的决定 不是吗?
but we've all had to make some tough calls, huh?

36
00:03:13,831 --> 00:03:14,331
快走!
Go!

37
00:03:14,664 --> 00:03:15,873
进行第二阶段
Move to phase two.

38
00:03:17,039 --> 00:03:20,498
伙计们 她必须到宝库那儿去
Guys, She has to go to the Vault.

39
00:03:21,248 --> 00:03:25,539
其实 这是个我们没考虑过的风险
That's actually a risk we haven't considered.

40
00:03:25,998 --> 00:03:28,331
我们费尽心思要宝库保持封闭
We've been so worried about keeping the Vault closed

41
00:03:28,373 --> 00:03:31,248
但我们从没想过利用宝库里的东西
that we never considered using what's inside.

42
00:03:31,456 --> 00:03:32,789
创造神杖
The Staff of Creation.

43
00:03:32,831 --> 00:03:34,956
或许我们可以用它来拯救Penny
Maybe we could use it to save Penny

44
00:03:34,998 --> 00:03:38,039
还可以保证擎天和曼特的人们安全
and get everyone in Atlas and Mantle back to safety.

45
00:03:42,623 --> 00:03:45,789
你们绝对猜不到是谁联系我了
Well, you'll never guess who I just heard from.

46
00:03:49,373 --> 00:03:52,206
所以 你不逮捕我?
So, you're not arresting me?

47
00:03:52,248 --> 00:03:52,706
不
No.

48
00:03:54,081 --> 00:03:55,831
有人得去阻止埃隆伍德
Ironwood's got to be stopped.

49
00:03:56,956 --> 00:03:57,956
那 你为什么打我?
Then, why did you hit me?

50
00:03:57,998 --> 00:04:00,873
因为如果我不做什么的话 你就要被杀了
Because you were about to get killed if I didn't do something.

51
00:04:07,123 --> 00:04:08,289
你在干什么?
What are you doing?

52
00:04:09,581 --> 00:04:11,248
我很久以前就该做的
What I should've done ages ago,

53
00:04:11,789 --> 00:04:13,456
联系我的妹妹
getting in touch with my sister.

54
00:04:13,873 --> 00:04:15,331
我们需要帮助
We're going to need help.

55
00:04:17,998 --> 00:04:18,706
啊?
Huh?

56
00:04:19,831 --> 00:04:21,164
说起帮助
Speaking of help.

57
00:04:21,706 --> 00:04:24,123
所以 人们被困在擎天和曼特城中
So, we've got people trapped in Atlas and Mantle

58
00:04:24,164 --> 00:04:26,539
要是不使用神杖的话就没法撤离
that we can't evacuate unless we use the Staff,

59
00:04:27,206 --> 00:04:29,206
而神杖就在宝库之中
which is located inside the Vault.

60
00:04:29,706 --> 00:04:32,539
如果我们打开了宝库 Penny就会自毁
we open the Vault, Penny terminates

61
00:04:33,081 --> 00:04:36,289
如果埃隆伍德听到了风声 他就会炸了曼特
If Ironwood gets wind of any of this, he blows up Mantle.

62
00:04:36,331 --> 00:04:37,831
还有其他事情需要考虑
There's something else to consider.

63
00:04:38,956 --> 00:04:40,873
一旦神杖用来创造别的东西
Oncethe Staff creates anything else,

64
00:04:41,289 --> 00:04:42,373
整个城市就会落下去
the city drops.

65
00:04:43,039 --> 00:04:45,123
就算擎天有足够的重力尘晶
Atlas has enough natural Gravity Dust

66
00:04:45,164 --> 00:04:46,706
能够防止它快速坠落
to keep it from plummeting immediately

67
00:04:46,831 --> 00:04:51,956
但也没人想在城市落地的时候站在那附近
but, well, nobody's going to want to be around when it touches down.

68
00:04:55,039 --> 00:04:58,581
好吧 那我们就用神杖来把所有人传送到安全的地方
Okay, then let's use the Staff to teleport everyone to safety.

69
00:04:59,123 --> 00:05:00,623
甚至可能是别的王国
Maybe even to another kingdom.

70
00:05:00,664 --> 00:05:02,623
我们不能就像挥舞魔杖一样
We can't just wave it like a magic wand

71
00:05:02,664 --> 00:05:04,206
来用它解决我们的问题
and make our problems go away.

72
00:05:04,664 --> 00:05:07,456
而且我们还没有和你们说起过他
And we haven't even told you about him.

73
00:05:07,873 --> 00:05:08,373
谁?
Who?

74
00:05:09,289 --> 00:05:10,581
在神杖中的精灵
The spirit in the Staff.

75
00:05:11,289 --> 00:05:15,206
就像珍 但是 他有点个性
Like Jinn but, well, he's a character.

76
00:05:15,581 --> 00:05:16,706
他可以创造任何东西
He can build you anything,

77
00:05:16,748 --> 00:05:19,414
但是要你给他解释怎么做
but only if you can explain to him how.

78
00:05:19,831 --> 00:05:21,914
就像工匠一样 他需要蓝图
Like any craftsman, he'll need blueprints.

79
00:05:22,206 --> 00:05:23,289
某种意义上的参考
Some sort of reference.

80
00:05:23,831 --> 00:05:26,373
如果我们能拿现实世界的例子给他的话会很有帮助
It'll help if we have real world examples to show him.

81
00:05:26,414 --> 00:05:28,164
我在疏散我家公司的时候
I've already gone through the city layouts

82
00:05:28,206 --> 00:05:29,748
拿到了城市平面图
for the SDC evacuation.

83
00:05:30,039 --> 00:05:31,123
或许我能帮忙?
Maybe I can help?

84
00:05:33,998 --> 00:05:36,539
那我们还需要考虑詹姆斯和他的炸弹
There's still James and his bomb to consider.

85
00:05:36,873 --> 00:05:38,414
噢 那个我有个计划
Oh, I've got a plan for that.

86
00:05:39,331 --> 00:05:41,748
那么 这可以解决第一阶段的问题
So, that takes care of phase one!

87
00:05:42,498 --> 00:05:47,331
与此同时 真Penny在我们的帮助下前往宝库
Meanwhile, the real Penny goes to the Vault with help.

88
00:05:47,831 --> 00:05:49,581
我在擎天的底部炸开了一个洞
I blasted a hole through the bottom of Atlas

89
00:05:49,706 --> 00:05:52,248
而且我怀疑他们没时间来修这个洞
and I highly doubt they've had time for repairs.

90
00:05:53,206 --> 00:05:54,789
你们应该可以从这里进去
That should take you straight to it.

91
00:05:57,623 --> 00:06:00,539
这些 是简单的部分
All of that, is the easy part.

92
00:06:01,831 --> 00:06:03,248
一旦Penny打开了门
As soon as Penny opens the door,

93
00:06:03,581 --> 00:06:05,331
我们就冲进去把神杖抢到手
we go through, grab the Staff,

94
00:06:05,373 --> 00:06:07,331
然后终止她的自毁程序,
and stop her termination.

95
00:06:07,539 --> 00:06:09,789
Penny 坚持住 好吗
Just hang in there, Penny. Okay?

96
00:06:51,539 --> 00:06:56,164
看起来有人需要我的创造力!
It seems someone has come to engage my creative wiles!

97
00:06:56,748 --> 00:07:00,123
不过嘛 最好能比我之前的那个项目好
All l'll say is, it had better be worth it after my last project.

98
00:07:00,623 --> 00:07:01,789
一座浮空城?
A floating city?

99
00:07:02,831 --> 00:07:03,914
太无趣了
How pedestrian.

100
00:07:04,373 --> 00:07:06,581
嗨 呃 安布罗休思先生?
Hi, um, Mr. Ambrosius?

101
00:07:06,623 --> 00:07:08,706
先生 是这样的 是我们的朋友
Sir, listen, it's about our friend.

102
00:07:08,748 --> 00:07:10,706
她 她快死了
She's- she's dying.

103
00:07:11,206 --> 00:07:13,123
我觉得你是知道的
I'm going to go ahead and assume that you know

104
00:07:13,164 --> 00:07:14,164
将人起死回生
it's against the rules for me

105
00:07:14,206 --> 00:07:17,123
是违背我的原则的 所以...
to bring people back from dead so-

106
00:07:17,164 --> 00:07:18,373
这不是我们想要的
That's not what we want.

107
00:07:18,873 --> 00:07:21,748
她不是你说的那种普通女孩
She's not your typical girl.

108
00:07:31,831 --> 00:07:33,789
确实 她不是
So, she isn't!

109
00:07:33,831 --> 00:07:36,706
我很想知道创造她的人是谁
I'd love to meet whoever did this.

110
00:07:37,539 --> 00:07:39,206
啊 我知道了
Ah, I see.

111
00:07:41,498 --> 00:07:43,081
是有东西在侵蚀她
There's something eating away at her.

112
00:07:43,456 --> 00:07:46,706
我猜你们有一个拯救她的好方法
I'm guessing you think you have some clever plan to save her.

113
00:07:46,748 --> 00:07:50,206
要知道 我会给你们你们所要求的
Just know, I will give you exactly what you ask for

114
00:07:50,248 --> 00:07:53,331
但要是如果你们不满意 我不接受任何抱怨
and I don't want any complaining when it's not what you wanted.

115
00:07:54,748 --> 00:07:56,248
我们带了她的设计图
We brought her schematics.

116
00:07:57,081 --> 00:07:59,164
我们想让你造一个新版本的她
We want you to make a new version of her

117
00:07:59,498 --> 00:08:01,539
完全使用她原本的机械部分
using her exact same robot parts.

118
00:08:01,956 --> 00:08:05,539
你的用词很有趣 小姑娘
That was curiously worded, girl.

119
00:08:05,789 --> 00:08:08,039
一个完全的复制体会携带原本的病毒
An exact copy of her would include the virus.

120
00:08:08,748 --> 00:08:10,623
一个不携带病毒的完全复制体
An exact copy of her without the virus

121
00:08:10,664 --> 00:08:13,498
在你做别的东西的时候就会彻底消失
vould cease to exist the second you make something else

122
00:08:14,164 --> 00:08:16,706
我们想让她在我们身边更久一些
and we kinda wanna keep her around longer than that.

123
00:08:18,081 --> 00:08:20,331
你们有好好做功课啊
You've done your homework.

124
00:08:20,623 --> 00:08:23,414
我们想让你制造一个新版本的她
We want you to create a new version of her,

125
00:08:24,039 --> 00:08:27,331
使用她本就存在的机械部分
using her existing robotic parts

126
00:08:27,956 --> 00:08:29,748
并将病毒一起带走
taking the virus with them.

127
00:08:29,789 --> 00:08:30,581
嗯哼
Hmm.

128
00:08:32,581 --> 00:08:36,414
好吧 但如果我把她的机械部分都拿出来了
Okay, but if I take the robot parts out of her,

129
00:08:36,456 --> 00:08:38,706
那剩下的
that would leave,

130
00:08:39,081 --> 00:08:39,664
Penny
Penny.

131
00:08:40,164 --> 00:08:42,414
那个一直在那具身体里存在着的女孩
The girl who's always been there underneath it.

132
00:08:43,456 --> 00:08:44,039
嗯哼
Hmm.

133
00:08:44,331 --> 00:08:45,456
你不能毁坏任何东西
You can't destroy,

134
00:08:46,039 --> 00:08:47,414
那是违反规定的
it's against the rules.

135
00:08:47,748 --> 00:08:49,539
但你不会毁掉她
But you wouldn't be destroying her.

136
00:08:50,414 --> 00:08:51,873
她内在的灵魂才是真正的她
Her soul is who she is.

137
00:08:51,914 --> 00:08:55,164
机械部分只是多余的
The mechanical parts are just extra.

138
00:08:55,748 --> 00:08:58,831
但一个没有完整肉体的灵魂
But a soul without a complete body,

139
00:08:58,873 --> 00:09:00,539
会剩什么呢?
what would be left?

140
00:09:00,581 --> 00:09:01,456
我不知道
I don't know.

141
00:09:02,289 --> 00:09:05,748
我猜你得发挥你的想象力了
I guess you just have to get creative.

142
00:09:08,914 --> 00:09:10,206
我想我可以做些小小的
I suppose I could do a little,

143
00:09:10,248 --> 00:09:12,164
噢 再加上一些
oh, add a touch of,

144
00:09:12,206 --> 00:09:12,956
但如果我那么做
but if I do that,

145
00:09:12,998 --> 00:09:14,998
有多少曾经的Penny会是我创造的
how much of the old Penny would be my work

146
00:09:15,039 --> 00:09:17,164
又有多少是她自己呢?
and how much would be her?

147
00:09:17,748 --> 00:09:19,498
那即将浮出水面了
Just coming up to the surface.

148
00:09:19,956 --> 00:09:21,998
这可太令人激动了
This is all very exciting,

149
00:09:22,414 --> 00:09:23,123
并且非常危险
and very dangerous

150
00:09:23,164 --> 00:09:26,456
我不知道结果会怎样
I don't know what the results are going to be.

151
00:09:26,498 --> 00:09:28,873
我们没有别的办法了
We don't have any other options.

152
00:09:29,289 --> 00:09:30,498
我们相信她
We believe in her.

153
00:09:31,539 --> 00:09:35,623
那么 准备好了 现在就是见证艺术的时刻!
Then, ready yourselves to witness my artistry!

154
00:10:02,289 --> 00:10:03,289
完成
It's done.

155
00:10:12,914 --> 00:10:14,539
我猜那就是信号了
I guess that's the signal then.

156
00:10:14,956 --> 00:10:16,748
看来宝库那边的进度不错
Seems like things are moving forward in the Vault.

157
00:10:16,789 --> 00:10:18,498
希望Penny不会有事
Hopefully Penny is going to be okay.

158
00:10:18,539 --> 00:10:21,581
如果擎天正在移动 我们需要在人们开始恐慌前告诉大家
If Atlas is moving, we need to get word out before people panic.

159
00:10:21,623 --> 00:10:22,998
所以快点!
Meaning hurry!

160
00:10:23,039 --> 00:10:23,748
知道了!知道了!
I know! I know!

161
00:10:24,164 --> 00:10:26,206
好了 这样应该就 呃
Okay, this should be, um,

162
00:10:27,456 --> 00:10:29,581
那应该 呃 有些什么作用?
that did, uh, something?

163
00:10:29,914 --> 00:10:30,498
你在直播
You're live.

164
00:10:31,039 --> 00:10:32,998
所有人都能看见你
Everyone can see you.

165
00:10:33,873 --> 00:10:34,539
哦哦!
Oh!

166
00:10:36,331 --> 00:10:37,873
擎天的人民
Citizens of Atlas,

167
00:10:38,206 --> 00:10:38,748
和曼特城
Mantle,

168
00:10:39,539 --> 00:10:41,623
我们需要告诉你们一件非常重要的事
what we have to tell you is very important.

169
00:10:41,956 --> 00:10:44,831
擎天正在坠落 但是
Atlas is falling but--

170
00:10:48,331 --> 00:10:50,164
等等 发生什么了?
Wait, what happened?

171
00:10:50,206 --> 00:10:50,873
断掉了
It's dead.

172
00:10:51,289 --> 00:10:53,873
整个泛大陆通讯系统直接停止了
The entire CCT, it just went down.

173
00:10:53,914 --> 00:10:57,081
王国内的通讯也是
And so did kingdom wide communications.

174
00:10:57,331 --> 00:10:58,206
怎么会?
How?

175
00:10:58,456 --> 00:11:01,331
更重要的是 我们现在怎么办?
The bigger question is, what do we do now?

176
00:11:02,248 --> 00:11:04,164
那小子说擎天正在坠落
That boy said Atlas is falling.

177
00:11:04,831 --> 00:11:05,789
是真的吗?
Is that true?

178
00:11:05,831 --> 00:11:08,831
是的 我们正在用神杖带领大家去到安全的地方
Yes. We're using the Staff to get everyone to safety.

179
00:11:09,331 --> 00:11:10,789
塞伦可以拿走那片废墟
Salem can have the rubble.

180
00:11:11,123 --> 00:11:12,456
那时我们早都离开了
We'll all be long gone.

181
00:11:12,998 --> 00:11:13,873
你
Are you,

182
00:11:14,331 --> 00:11:16,039
你要把我留在这儿吗?
are you going to leave me here?

183
00:11:18,206 --> 00:11:18,831
不
No.

184
00:11:19,789 --> 00:11:22,289
我们完工后会把你们两个带去安全区域
When we're finished, we'll move both of you to safety.

185
00:11:22,873 --> 00:11:25,164
噢 温特 谢谢你
Oh Winter, thank you.

186
00:11:25,206 --> 00:11:25,581
我
I--

187
00:11:25,623 --> 00:11:26,581
别谢我
Don't thank me.

188
00:11:27,164 --> 00:11:29,289
这是Weiss决定的
It was Weiss's decision.

189
00:11:38,081 --> 00:11:38,873
Penny?
Penny?

190
00:12:11,956 --> 00:12:13,873
你还好吗?
Are you okay?

191
00:12:18,331 --> 00:12:21,914
每次拥抱时身体里都会暖呼呼的吗?
Do hugs always make you feel this warm inside?

192
00:12:23,248 --> 00:12:24,039
是的
Yes.

193
00:12:24,456 --> 00:12:25,873
哇!
Wow!

194
00:12:27,664 --> 00:12:28,581
还要!
More!

195
00:12:28,623 --> 00:12:31,706
我们最好还是确认一下我们的理论可行
We should probably make sure our theory worked.

196
00:12:34,206 --> 00:12:35,998
然后开始撤离
And start the evacuation.

197
00:12:40,498 --> 00:12:41,206
啊!
Ah!

198
00:12:41,289 --> 00:12:45,664
自由地创造与 哦 又是你们
Free to create and, oh, it's you guys again.

199
00:12:45,914 --> 00:12:47,331
我们找你还有事
We're not done with you yet.

200
00:12:47,373 --> 00:12:48,914
呃 行吧!
Ugh, fine!

201
00:12:48,956 --> 00:12:50,164
试试简洁的版本吧
Let's try the quick version.

202
00:12:50,206 --> 00:12:51,998
你你不能在擎天创造一大堆门
Can you make a bunch of doorways in Atlas

203
00:12:52,039 --> 00:12:53,831
然后全都连接到真空王国的一处?
that open at a single spot in Vacuo?

204
00:12:53,873 --> 00:12:54,706
行啊!
Sure!

205
00:12:54,748 --> 00:12:57,081
我只需要每个门的坐标和规格
I'll just need coordinates and specs for each door,

206
00:12:57,123 --> 00:12:58,706
一个扭曲时空与时间的解释方法
an explanation for bending space and time

207
00:12:58,748 --> 00:13:00,914
由此来解决单向通行数量过多
to account for the much greater traffic on one side,

208
00:13:00,956 --> 00:13:02,914
以及另一边只有一个出口的问题
and the single point of exit on the other.

209
00:13:02,998 --> 00:13:04,873
好吧 这我们也猜到了
ay, that's about what we expect

210
00:13:05,248 --> 00:13:07,123
所以 我们需要运送所有人
So, we need to funnel everybody

211
00:13:07,164 --> 00:13:08,581
先到达到一个中心地点
through a central location first.

212
00:13:08,998 --> 00:13:10,248
你得多跟我说说这个
You're going to have to tell me more

213
00:13:10,289 --> 00:13:11,581
中心地点
about this central location.

214
00:13:11,623 --> 00:13:14,164
首先 呃 它在哪?
For starters, uh, where is it?

215
00:13:14,623 --> 00:13:18,498
这儿 一个类似这些宝库的地方
Here. A place like these Vaults.

216
00:13:19,123 --> 00:13:21,456
不论它们在哪 他们并不是树不子的一部分
Wherever they are, they're not part of Remnant.

217
00:13:21,914 --> 00:13:24,498
只有在你知道怎么去的时候才能到达
Only accessible if you know the right way in.

218
00:13:25,123 --> 00:13:27,914
听起来像是个对于成干上万难民来说足够安全的地方
Seems like a safe enough place for thousands of refugees.

219
00:13:28,581 --> 00:13:31,456
你们这帮熊孩子要么是特别聪明
You kids are either smart

220
00:13:31,664 --> 00:13:34,289
要么就是超出自己想象的蠢
or much more foolish than you realize.

221
00:13:35,498 --> 00:13:37,123
我需要个参考
I'm going to need a reference?

222
00:13:37,164 --> 00:13:38,831
哦 我们有
Oh, we've got one.

223
00:14:17,081 --> 00:14:19,831
擎天和曼特城的人从一端进入
People enter from Atlas and Mantle on one side,

224
00:14:25,373 --> 00:14:26,831
然后从另一端出来
and leave on the other side,

225
00:14:26,873 --> 00:14:28,623
一张通往真空王国的单程票
with a one-way ticket to Vacuo.

226
00:14:30,414 --> 00:14:33,581
一切好像都就位了
Well, everything appears to be in order.

227
00:14:33,623 --> 00:14:35,664
你们说的非常清晰
You were quite thorough,

228
00:14:36,248 --> 00:14:37,456
真让人不爽
disappointingly so.

229
00:14:38,914 --> 00:14:40,498
所以 这就好了?
So, it's done?

230
00:14:40,956 --> 00:14:42,123
是啊
Yeah.

231
00:14:49,456 --> 00:14:52,123
哦对 最后一个小小的说明
Oh, and one last point of clarification

232
00:14:52,164 --> 00:14:55,289
关于你这个中心点
about this central location of yours,

233
00:14:56,623 --> 00:14:58,456
别落下
do not fall.

234
00:15:00,289 --> 00:15:03,831
好了 恐怖的警示也给完了
Okay, and with that dire warning.

235
00:15:15,289 --> 00:15:16,123
我们做到了!
We did it!

236
00:15:17,623 --> 00:15:19,289
现在呢?
What now?

237
00:15:19,664 --> 00:15:20,998
我们去真空
We go to Macuo,

238
00:15:22,539 --> 00:15:23,539
大家一起
all of us,

239
00:15:27,123 --> 00:15:29,206
希望我们考虑到了所有方面
and hope that we've thought of everything.